**(i) Green computing (2 marks).** Green computing (green IT) is the study and practice of designing, manufacturing, using and disposing of computers and related devices in a way that reduces their harm to the environment, by saving energy and reducing electronic waste.

**(ii) Two ways to enhance it (2 marks, 1 mark each).** Any two of:

- switch off computers or use sleep mode when they are not in use;
- buy energy-efficient equipment (for example LED screens, low-power processors);
- recycle or reuse old computers, batteries and cartridges instead of throwing them away;
- print less and use electronic documents;
- share resources through virtualisation or cloud services so that fewer machines are needed.
